    t: 'evid',
    p: 'In Cora Whitcombe\'s 1924 novel The Lamplighter\'s Daughter, the narrator, Agnes, describes the day her classmate Margaret wins first prize in a regional painting competition. Throughout the scene, Agnes conceals her intense envy of Margaret beneath a show of indifference.',
    q: 'Which quotation from The Lamplighter\'s Daughter most effectively illustrates the claim?',
